k);\n  content.dataset.scale = k.toFixed(3);\n  if (k !== 1) content.style.transform = `scale(${k})`;", "start": 1, "title": ""}}, "says": [{"id": "fit.1.2", "status": "ready", "text": "The old code reset and applied CSS zoom. Under zoom, text-range bounding boxes come back in the wrong coordinate space, so the pointer missed. The new code [clears the transform](# \"transform = \"\"\"), then measures the natural size, taking the larger of offset and scroll width. It computes a scale, snaps near-one values to exactly one, clamps at zero point three, and applies it as a transform. The scale is also stored on the element so the measure script can read it.", "cues": [{"at": 13, "end": 30, "label": "reset and applied", "target": "", "text": "zoom", "kind": "text", "t": 0.975}, {"at": 205, "end": 230, "label": "measures the natural size", "target": "", "text": "Math.max(content.offsetWidth", "kind": "text", "t": 11.15}, {"at": 290, "end": 297, "label": "a scale", "target": "", "text": "let k", "kind": "text", "t": 15.938}, {"at": 321, "end": 335, "label": "to exactly one", "target": "", "text": "k = 1;", "kind": "text", "t": 18.05}, {"at": 347, "end": 363, "label": "zero point three", "target": "", "text": "Math.max(0.3, k)", "kind": "text", "t": 19.788}, {"at": 369, "end": 379, "label": "applies it", "target": "", "text": "scale(${k})", "kind": "text", "t": 21.087}, {"at": 414, "end": 435, "label": "stored on the element", "target": "", "text": "dataset.scale", "kind": "text", "t": 24.15}], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/468fc183a1bfb1abe6b9c764.mp3", "duration": 27.15, "words": [{"s": 0.25, "e": 0.375, "c0": 0, "c1": 3}, {"s": 0.375, "e": 0.625, "c0": 4, "c1": 7}, {"s": 0.625, "e": 0.975, "c0": 8, "c1": 12}, {"s": 0.975, "e": 1.425, "c0": 13, "c1": 18}, {"s": 1.425, "e": 1.538, "c0": 19, "c1": 22}, {"s": 1.538, "e": 1.962, "c0": 23, "c1": 30}, {"s": 1.962, "e": 2.525, "c0": 31, "c1": 34}, {"s": 2.525, "e": 3.225, "c0": 35, "c1": 39}, {"s": 3.35, "e": 3.625, "c